course: dictionary
lesson: 627
title: Babyish and childish
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how old something seems. Babyish means like a baby, or too young for someone older. Read the words around it to find its meaning: «Tom in Sydney thought his bike helmet looked babyish and left it at home.» Tom did not want to look too young for his age, so babyish means too young-looking for someone his age.
explain: Babyish can describe things, like toys, books or shows, and it can describe behaviour. Babyish behaviour is acting silly or childish in a way that is not right for your age. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "Tom thought his helmet looked too young for him" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Notice the feeling behind the word. Calling someone babyish can be hurtful, because everyone likes different things. «Liking things others call babyish is fine; "you do you" is slang for be yourself.» The context shows that babyish is someone's opinion, so you should think before you use it about a person.
explain: Other words have a similar meaning, such as childish and immature. Childish is very close to babyish, while immature means not yet grown up in how you think or behave. When context is not enough, a dictionary helps you check the exact meaning.
fact: Babyish means like a baby, or too young for someone older.
fact: Babyish behaviour is silly or childish, and not right for your age.
fact: «Fear of needles is very common in both children and adults, and it isn't babyish.» Feeling scared of needles is normal, so it is not babyish.
fact: Similar words: childish and immature.
fact: Calling someone babyish can hurt them, because everyone likes different things.
exercise: «Tom in Sydney thought his bike helmet looked babyish and left it at home.» What does babyish mean here? | *Too young-looking for someone his age | Bright red and brand new | Made of soft plastic | Very fast and shiny
exercise: «Fear of needles is very common in both children and adults, and it isn't babyish.» What does this tell us? | Only babies are scared of needles | Adults should never feel scared | *Feeling scared of needles is normal, not too young for someone older | Needles are babyish toys
exercise: Ava's friends say Mia's pony stickers are «giving baby». What does this Gen Alpha phrase mean? | *Looks babyish | Looks very expensive | Is a famous brand | Is hidden under a coat
test: Which word has a similar meaning to babyish? | Curt | Famished | *Childish | Luminous
test: Why might calling someone babyish be unkind? | *Because everyone likes different things, and it can hurt their feelings | Because it means very old | Because it is a very long word | Because babies are always rude
exam: Ella says, «Liking things others call babyish is fine.» Why is she right? | Only grown-ups are allowed to like things | Babyish means dangerous | *Everyone likes different things, and being yourself is fine | Babyish means happy
